.TH CHTTPSVR_ENGINE_STOP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_engine_stop \- signal the engine to stop
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

void chttpsvr_engine_stop(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Signals chttpserver's own shared reactor (and its companion
idle-timeout sweep thread) to stop, forcing it down even if other
chttpsvr instances in the same process still hold a reference.  This
reactor is independent of chttpclient's own engine, so calling this
function has no effect on any chttpclient async work
(chttpclient_do_async/_streaming, chttpclient_do_pooled/_streaming) in
the same process.  Returns immediately; use chttpsvr_engine_wait() to
block until the stop completes.

Non-blocking and async-signal-safe: it is safe to call this function
directly from a POSIX signal handler (e.g. SIGINT, SIGTERM).

The library does not install any signal handlers.  Applications are
responsible for wiring this function into whatever signal or shutdown
mechanism they use.

Safe to call before the reactor has ever started (no-op).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3),
.BR chttpsvr_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_start (3)
